Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Revised strategy: aggressively guarantee well-formed arithmetic delimiters.
// The prior attempt could open a constrained span too eagerly and then run out
// of steps before emitting the matching ">>", causing unterminated spans and a
// syntax-rate failure. The new policy only opens a span when there is enough
// remaining budget to both produce at least one constrained token and then close
// the span later, and it prioritizes closing whenever the parser says the span
// is complete. Outside constrained mode, the decoder strongly prefers opening
// only on explicit evidence (the sampled token is "<<" or "<<" is the argmax)
// rather than on a loose logit threshold. Inside constrained mode, it always
// uses parser-valid next-token generation and never treats ">>" as ordinary span
// content; instead, closing is performed only from the parser-complete branch.
// Finally, if the loop reaches its last available step while still inside a
// constrained span, it refuses to append more constrained content and exits,
// preventing creation of a fresh unterminated segment under the method's step
// bound. This directly targets the observed evaluation failure mode.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the unconstrained branch, either we remain outside
//   constrained mode (so the implication is vacuous), or we open a span via
//   OpenConstrainedSpan, which sets currentConstrainedOut to [] and therefore a
//   valid parser prefix. In the inside/complete branch, CloseConstrainedSpan
//   exits constrained mode, making the implication vacuous. In the inside /
//   not-complete append branch, the next token comes from ConstrainedStep, which
//   is parser-valid on non-EOS, and AppendConstrainedToken preserves validity.
//   In the early-break branch on the last step, state is unchanged.
// suffix: Outside constrained mode the invariant is vacuous unless we open a
//   span; OpenConstrainedSpan appends "<<" to generated and sets the tracked
//   constrained content to [], so the empty suffix matches. In the close branch,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan resets constrained tracking to [], so the implication is
//   vacuous. In the constrained append branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends the
//   same token to generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving the suffix
//   relationship. In the break branch, no state changes.
// cost: OpenConstrainedSpan, ConstrainedStep, CloseConstrainedSpan, and
//   UnconstrainedStep each internally bump helpers.cost by 1, and each such
//   branch also increments steps once. Query-only operations do not bump cost.
//   The raw unconstrained sampling branch is avoided entirely, so there is no
