Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The previous strategy achieved good answer accuracy but poor syntax because it
// sometimes let the model write non-arithmetic text inside `<< >>`, such as
// variable names or prose. To fix that, this revision makes constrained spans
// much stricter and more targeted.
//
// Main changes:
// 1. Outside constrained mode, we no longer opportunistically open on arbitrary
//    tokens merely containing "<<". We only open when the chosen token is exactly
//    "<<" or when "<<" is the current argmax after a strong boost. This reduces
//    malformed delimiter behavior.
// 2. Inside constrained mode, we never use the old argmax fast path. Instead we
//    always generate through `ConstrainedStep`, so every token inside `<< >>` is
//    parser-filtered arithmetic syntax.
// 3. We close a constrained span immediately once the parser says the arithmetic
//    prefix is complete, and we also bias toward opening a new constrained span
//    whenever the free-form model appears ready to emit digits or operators.
//    This encourages step-by-step arithmetic computations to be isolated inside
//    delimiters, improving syntax rate while preserving answer quality.
// 4. We keep EOS terminal and maintain the same explicit tracking discipline:
//    `generated` stores the full answer including delimiters, while
//    `currentConstrainedOut` stores only the active arithmetic contents.
//
// Overall, the strategy is: free-form explanation outside spans, parser-only
// arithmetic inside spans, and eager close once a valid arithmetic computation
// is complete.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the outside-span branch, either we append an ordinary
//   token and remain outside (so the implication is vacuous), or we open a span
//   with `OpenConstrainedSpan`, which sets the constrained content to `[]`,
//   valid by precondition. In the inside-span branch, if the current prefix is
//   complete we close with `CloseConstrainedSpan`, making the implication
//   vacuous; otherwise `ConstrainedStep` is followed by `AppendConstrainedToken`
//   only when the sampled token is parser-valid-next, so validity is preserved.
// suffix: Outside a span the invariant is vacuous. Opening a span appends the
//   delimiter but leaves constrained content empty, so the empty suffix matches.
//   Closing a span resets constrained content to `[]`, so the implication is
//   vacuous again. Appending a parser-valid constrained token extends both
//   `generated` and `currentConstrainedOut` by the same token, preserving the
//   suffix equality.
// cost: In the outside branch we either call `OpenConstrainedSpan` or manually
//   sample with `ChooseNextTokenUnconstrained` and then increment
//   `helpers.cost` once; in the inside branch we either call
//   `CloseConstrainedSpan` or `ConstrainedStep`, both of which bump helper cost
//   by 1 internally. Every non-breaking iteration also increments `steps` by 1,
//   and pure queries/logit adjustments do not change helper cost, so
//   `helpers.cost <= steps` is preserved.
// progress: Each non-breaking iteration appends at most one token to
//   `generated`: an unconstrained token, the opening delimiter from
//   `OpenConstrainedSpan`, one constrained token via `AppendConstrainedToken`, or
//   the closing delimiter from `CloseConstrainedSpan`. Since `steps` increases by
//   1 on every such iteration, `|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps` is
//   maintained; on EOS break, `generated` does not grow further.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;
helpers.cost := 0;

var steps := 0;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  invariant cost == 0
  invariant helpers.cost <= steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
